# Build the deepest Twilight Huntsman this game allows and photograph his
# [L]earn Spells menu. bd inc-tek.8.3 finding PA-03-F22, and bd inc-f34.
#
# WHAT THIS SCRIPT PROVED, and it is not what it set out to prove. The
# huntsman's printed spell list names bestow curse at 3rd level
# (lib/prestige.irh:2916) and his SPELL_LIST omitted it. The spell was added
# (lib/prestige.irh:2977). NO CHARACTER CAN SEE THAT, and three numbers say
# so before any run does:
#
#   * A caster needs caster level 5 to learn a 3rd-level spell. The Learn
#     Spells menu skips any spell whose SAL exceeds AbilityLevel(
#     CA_SPELLCASTING) (src/Create.cpp:4505-4507), and __SAL is
#     { 0, 1, 3, 5, 7, 9, 12, 14, 16, 18 } (src/Tables.cpp:48).
#   * The huntsman gains one caster level at every 2nd class level
#     (lib/prestige.irh:2953), so caster level 5 needs TEN class levels.
#   * No prestige class may be taken before three core levels
#     (src/Managers.cpp:2251), and MAX_CHAR_LEVEL is 11
#     (inc/Defines.h:4367). 10 + 3 = 13.
#
# So the 3rd, 4th and 5th level entries of this class's spell list are dead
# data in this build, and the bestow curse fix is Traced, not Observed. This
# script is kept because it builds the deepest huntsman the rules allow --
# three core levels, which is the engine minimum, and eight class levels,
# which is every level the cap leaves -- and it becomes the oracle the day
# the cap moves. He reaches caster level 4, one short.
#
# THE THREE-LEVEL ENTRY. The gate wants Ride 8, Athletics 8, Hide 5, Move
# Silently 5, Animal Empathy 5 and Maeve (lib/prestige.irh:2807-2827). The
# ranger carries every one of those skills except Athletics, and three ranger
# levels buy six ranks in each, which clears them all once the attribute and
# training terms are added.
#
# ATHLETICS COMES FROM A FEAT. Natural Aptitude (src/FeatTab.cpp:60) is
# FF_MULTIPLE, so it can be taken again and again, and each one grants an
# EXTRA_SKILL stati with source SS_CLAS (src/Create.cpp:2832).
# Character::MaxRanks (src/Create.cpp:3802-3810) answers such a stati with
# ClassLevelRanks[TotalLevel()] -- the full character-level cap, the same
# term a racial skill gets, and it does not care which classes the character
# holds. One feat therefore replaces the three rogue levels the older script
# spent on Athletics.
#
# WHY A RANGER AND NOT A ROGUE, which would also carry Athletics.
# Character::XPPenalty (src/Create.cpp:2196-2199) reads
# TCLASS(ClassID[2])->HasFlag(CF_FAVOURED) without checking that a third
# class exists, and RES(0) is NULL. A two-class character reaches that line
# whenever his first class is not favoured for his race AND his
# CF_FAVOURED class is not his highest. An Elf Rogue 3 / Twilight Huntsman 1
# is exactly that, and drawing his sheet segfaults. The ranger is a favoured
# class of elves (lib/races.irh:967), so he answers the first test while he
# is the higher of the two, and the huntsman -- which is CF_FAVOURED -- answers
# the second test from his 4th level on. The null line is never reached.
#
# An elf is given Maeve at birth (lib/races.irh:1144-1147).
#
# THE ORACLE is the [L]earn Spells menu, which src/Create.cpp:4356-4375
# builds by walking the SPELL_ACCESS stati and reading each granting
# resource's SPELL_LIST. The menu is that list, filtered by caster level.
#
# SEED. The attribute rolls and the offered feats vary with the seed, so the
# feat picks stay positional and a seed is passed.

a       # Initial Choices: [a] Create a New Character
n       # Alter the character generation options? -- no
y       # Your options will place the game in Explore Mode. Continue? -- yes

@choose "Elf"
@choose "Elf (Standard)"
@choose "Ranger"
a                       # Attributes: the first of the offered sets
@choose "Neutral"
@choose "Goblinkin"     # favoured enemy
a                       # combat style: [a] archery

# The menu truncates the label to fit its column, so the name matched here
# is the truncated one. @choose reads what is drawn, not what it stands for.
@choose "Natural Aptitud"       # the feat that opens the gate
@choose "Athletics"             # and the skill it opens it with
@until "Unspent Skill Ranks" a  # however many further feats are asked for

# Twelve ranks, two to a skill, taken in the order the list prints them so
# the view only ever scrolls forward. @cursorto:mark reads the visible page,
# and a mark that has already scrolled off the top cannot be found again.
@cursorto:mark "Animal Empathy" DOWN
RIGHT*2
@cursorto:mark "Hide in Shadows" DOWN
RIGHT*2
@cursorto:mark "Listen" DOWN
RIGHT*2
@cursorto:mark "Move Silently" DOWN
RIGHT*2
@cursorto:mark "Ride" DOWN
RIGHT*2
@cursorto:mark "Searching" DOWN
RIGHT*2
ENTER y # Done, and confirm keeping the ranks

a       # Personality archetype

ESC     # dismiss the arrival-room description; now in play
w       # wizard mode
y       # "Enter wizard mode?" -- yes
w       # [w] Wizard Mode Switches
DOWN DOWN
SPACE   # Free Advancement: NO -> YES
ESC

d                               # character sheet
@until "Class  Ranger 3" G      # three core levels, and no class menu:
                                #   Player::AdvanceLevel only asks which
                                #   class when a second one exists.

# Fill the gate skills to their caps.
S
@expect "Unspent Skill Ranks"

# In the order the list prints them. The ranger's own skills come first,
# alphabetically; Athletics is not one of his, so the feat's grant is
# appended after them and has to be marked last.
@cursorto:mark "Animal Empathy" DOWN
RIGHT*8
@cursorto:mark "Hide in Shadows" DOWN
RIGHT*8
@cursorto:mark "Move Silently" DOWN
RIGHT*8
@cursorto:mark "Ride" DOWN
RIGHT*8
@cursorto:mark "Athletics" DOWN
RIGHT*8
ENTER y

P                               # [P]restige Classes
@expect "Choose a class:"
@choose "Twilight Huntsman"
@expect "Huntsman 0"            # the gate let him in

# Eight huntsman levels, which is every level the character cap leaves.
# The sheet does not repaint while a level-up menu is open, so a directive
# that only reads the screen would be looking at a picture of the old
# character. @until presses a key on every pass, which answers the menu and
# lets the sheet repaint. 'a' is Strength on the attribute menu and the first
# entry on the feat menu, and it is not a character-sheet command, so the
# presses that land on the sheet do nothing.
@until "class do you wish to advance" G
@choose "Twilight Huntsman"
@until "Huntsman 1" a
@until "class do you wish to advance" G
@choose "Twilight Huntsman"
@until "Huntsman 2" a
@until "class do you wish to advance" G
@choose "Twilight Huntsman"
@until "Huntsman 3" a
@until "class do you wish to advance" G
@choose "Twilight Huntsman"
@until "Huntsman 4" a
@until "class do you wish to advance" G
@choose "Twilight Huntsman"
@until "Huntsman 5" a
@until "class do you wish to advance" G
@choose "Twilight Huntsman"
@until "Huntsman 6" a
@until "class do you wish to advance" G
@choose "Twilight Huntsman"
@until "Huntsman 7" a
@until "class do you wish to advance" G
@choose "Twilight Huntsman"
@until "Huntsman 8" a

W                       # Write Dump
c u r s e ENTER         # filename: "curse"

L                       # [L]earn Spells -- the spell list oracle
@dump:learn3
ESC
ESC
@quit
